<% content_for :title, @stock.ticker %>

<%# Stock detail.

    This page had escaped every earlier sweep, and it showed:

    - a hand-rolled header (h1 + an actions row) where every other page in the app renders
      components/ui/_page_header, so it also never declared :own_heading
    - a decorative emoji pair beside the h1
    - the archived state as a hand-rolled bg-red-100/text-red-800 rounded-full pill instead of
      components/ui/_badge
    - py-6 on top of main's own p-4 lg:p-6, and a <div class="h-8"> spacer under the content
    - one more </div> than it opened
    - flex-shrink-0 and HTML comments, where the app uses shrink-0 and ERB comments

    The company name moves into the header's description, and the ticker is the title. It used to
    be one h1 reading "AAPL | Apple Inc." with the company name in a nested span at a smaller
    size - a two-part heading held together by a pipe. %>
<div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl">
  <%# The badge goes under the title, not inside the h1 - the same reason admin/teachers#show
      records: inside the heading it becomes part of the page's accessible name. %>
  <% description = @stock.company_name %>
  <% if @stock.archived? %>
    <% badge = render("components/ui/badge", label: "Archived", tone: :danger) %>
    <% description = safe_join([description, badge], " ") %>
  <% end %>

  <%= render layout: "components/ui/page_header",
             locals: { title: @stock.ticker, description: description } do %>
    <%= link_to "Back to trading floor", stocks_path, class: "tw-btn-secondary" %>

    <%# The page's own trade action. It used to be a primary "Trade" that navigated to the
        trading floor - the same destination as the back link beside it - so a stock's page
        could not act on that stock. This is the trading floor's own Buy/Sell partial behind
        the same policy gate, which keeps one definition of the product's core transaction and
        opens the order modal for this stock. %>
    <% if policy(@stock).show_trading_link? %>
      <%= render "stocks/trade_actions", stock: @stock %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>

  <%= render @stock %>
</div>
